        "source_sha256": "642928ffd1b7f9a3e8b6fe2f50cfee11af85ed24d2689a7d5cbd74e25f5795a0",
        "text": "# Joel Woods · Candidate for San Ramon Valley School Board\nStudents First. Always.\nOur schools are the foundation of the San Ramon Valley community.\nFor more than twenty years, Joel Woods has called the San Ramon Valley home and has seen firsthand how exceptional public schools strengthen our neighborhoods, support families, and create opportunities for our students.\nNow Joel is running for the San Ramon Valley Unified School District Board of Education to protect what makes our schools exceptional while ensuring the district remains academically strong, fiscally responsible, transparent, and responsive to the people it serves\n### The best decisions start by listening. Share what’s working, what needs attention, and what you want to see for the future of SRVUSD.\nShare Your Voice\nSupport Joel.$990$500$250$99$25Other\nWhat’s Best for Our Students Comes First\n### Protecting and Enhancing Academic Excellence\nOur students deserve a rigorous, balanced education that prepares them for college, vocational careers, and an evolving global economy.\n### Ensuring Fiscal Accountability and Classroom Priorities\nParents and taxpayers trust the district to manage public resources effectively. Every dollar should be evaluated by how it supports our schools and students.\n### Supporting Teachers and Staff\nGreat schools begin with great educators. Having worked within local classrooms, I understand how important it is for teachers and staff to feel supported, respected, and properly resourced.\n### Fostering Community Collaboration and Transparent Leadership\nSchool Board decisions should reflect the needs of the students and community the district serves. That requires listening before decisions are made, not simply communicating afterward.\nLearn More About My Priorities",
        "text_limited": false,
        "title": "Joel Woods for San Ramon Valley School Board",
